{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532404-blood-sigils-question","id":1532404,"title":"Blood Sigils Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-11T17:51:16-07:00","id":1532404,"title":"Blood Sigils Question","content":"Am I missing something with Blood Sigils? It feels like while this scene is cool that it would work better with Tremere at its old power. Since that would be the reason for the scene to be so underground/criminal. Or is there some faction I am missing for why the scene feels this way instead of closer to the old style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T18:02:53-07:00","id":1532405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532404-blood-sigils-question#post1532404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I missing something with Blood Sigils? It feels like while this scene is cool that it would work better with Tremere at its old power. Since that would be the reason for the scene to be so underground/criminal. Or is there some faction I am missing for why the scene feels this way instead of closer to the old style?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm doing my review of it now but I think Blood Sigils would make no sense with the Tremere at their former power. Basically, this is post-Soviet Union underworld, Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are gone so no one is stopping ANYONE who wants to learn magic from doing so.<br /> <br /> The reason the Scene exists is because there's a description for what happens to all the people dealing in illegal magic Pre-Vienna: ash.<br /> <br /> There's a power vacuum and now anyone can trade in sorcery but being Kindred they're murdering each other for the equivalent of cook books and drug labs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T18:29:02-07:00","id":1532408,"title":"","content":"Here's the review I did (obviously, I think OPP would have done better):<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">BLOOD SIGILS is a supplement for VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE FIFTH EDITION. It is a supplement detailing the use of Blood Sorcery, Thin Blooded Alchemy, and the black market that has emerged around the use of magic among vampires (called \u201cThe Scene\u201d).</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> Blood magic supplements were quite popular in earlier editions of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> and it is surprising its taken this long to have a book discussing its use. Could the book have contained more information on things like Oblivion and Church of Set magic? Probably but we\u2019ll mostly be judging the book on what it is rather than what it could be.</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><br /> <br /> Overall, I think <i>Blood Sigils</i> is one of the best books released by Renegade Studios so far. I was not fond of <i>The Second Inquisition</i> or<i> Sabbat: The Black Hand</i> supplements but was much more appreciative of <i>Blood-Stained Love</i>. <i>Blood Sigils</i> benefits from a decision that I hope more books will take heed from in the future: the decision to incorporate more lore from the classic era of Vampire: The Masquerade. Given so many other supplements seem interested in ignoring or quietly retconning classic lore, it\u2019s nice to see this book is best appreciated by those with a decades-long familiarity with the material.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Seriously, the book\u2019s best parts are updating both Clan Tremere and the Banu Haqim with references to their extensive history. Not just the now-destroyed chantry in Vienna is referenced but also House Ceoris from <i>Vampire: The Dark Ages</i>. \u201cHouse Goratrix\u201d has taken over the section of Clan Tremere that is attempting to rebuild the Pyramid as it used to be and its leader is someone that will be familiar to anyone familiar with The Transylvania Chronicles. We also get a sense of what happened with the Banu Haqim Schism that was the focus Clan Book: Assamite Revised.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This book is perfectly usable by players who have never experienced Vampire: The Masquerade before Fifth Edition and these are just interesting references. However, as Easter Eggs for those who have spent thirty years playing in the World of Darkness, they are a reminder that our fandom is appreciated. I could have done with even more but I\u2019m certainly not going to begrudge the book for including what it did. Sadly, those looking for updates of things like Thaumaturgy Paths and specific rituals will have to look elsewhere. The majority of the book is devoted to the creation of a thriving magical subculture in the wake of the Tremere\u2019s stranglehold being destroyed by the Second Inquisition.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Everyone who wants to learn magic can learn magic these days, at least among the Damned. But being the immortal parasites they are, this comes with a price. The majority of magic for sale is watered down, erroneous, or from copies of copies. Experimentation is the order of the day and back alley deals are happening in every major city.</span><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"> The central conceit of <i>Blood Sigils</i> is that magic is like drugs and especially drug dealing. Quality, ingredients, violence, crooked law enforcement (human or otherwise), and cheats are all things you run into in \u201cThe Scene.\u201d It is also strongly related to the Blood Trade where buying nourishment is significantly easier than buying the blood of a specific seven year old that was born under a blood moon. Much of the horror is implied and that is what makes it appropriately punk.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The book contains sample NPCs of dealers, crooked Sheriffs, crooked cops, dabblers, veterans, diablerists, and Thin Blooded alchemists. It contains a large number of blood cults and magical secret societies that vary in quality (my favorite is a Masquerade breaking pharmaceutical company from India). There\u2019s also several magical artifacts meant to show how they might be implemented into the setting. Much of the Storyteller advice is based on creating mood and, for once, actually quite useful.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Blood Sigils is probably the most \u201cpunk\u201d book that Fifth Edition has produced and actually reads like someone who has more than a television show\u2019s familiarity with drugs and the underground night life of a major city. Whether they have or not, it feels evocative and actually manages to live up to the potential of Fifth Edition. Paradox Interactive has continually wanted to capture an adult counter-culture feel for its middle aged veteran audience and newcomers alike. This actually succeeds.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T18:47:55-07:00","id":1532410,"title":"","content":"Edit: Never mind. Blood Sigils is available for preorder on Demiplane now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 03-14-2024, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T19:11:28-07:00","id":1532413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532404-blood-sigils-question?p=1532405#post1532405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm doing my review of it now but I think Blood Sigils would make no sense with the Tremere at their former power. Basically, this is post-Soviet Union underworld, Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Tremere are gone so no one is stopping ANYONE who wants to learn magic from doing so.<br /> <br /> The reason the Scene exists is because there's a description for what happens to all the people dealing in illegal magic Pre-Vienna: ash.<br /> <br /> There's a power vacuum and now anyone can trade in sorcery but being Kindred they're murdering each other for the equivalent of cook books and drug labs.</div> </div> </div> </div>If no ones stopping them then why does the blood magic underground need to be so criminal styled? Reading it gave Cyberpunk style vibes to me. Especially with pushing the blood magic into the same circles as cleaners and blood forgers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","user":"Dante","date":". 03-11-2024, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T19:59:10-07:00","id":1532415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532404-blood-sigils-question?p=1532413#post1532413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If no ones stopping them then why does the blood magic underground need to be so criminal styled? Reading it gave Cyberpunk style vibes to me. Especially with pushing the blood magic into the same circles as cleaners and blood forgers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my bad.<br /> <br /> I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> I think the answer presented in the book is the fact that with the Tremere monopoly broken, huge numbers of vampires from varying clans are competing for whatever can be harvested from defunct Tremere chantries and passed around among them. There's limited resources for grimoires, magical components, and other stuff that they're viciously fighting over or trading for scraps regarding.<br /> <br /> So, anyone can learn magic but there's not the formalized training or massive libraries that used to exist before (or at least the Tremere are keeping that on the D-Low). Instead, everyone is basically forced to assemble scrapbooks and share fragments of knowledge. Instead of a dozen master Tremere mages in America, there's a couple of hundred dabblers all trying to become more important and getting an edge.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim don't mind sharing their magic but they're not giving their best stuff. After all, a few level 1-2 rituals can mean the difference between final death and otherwise for a Brujah but mean shit for most Sorcerer Caste.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T20:29:05-07:00","id":1532417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532404-blood-sigils-question?p=1532415#post1532415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh my bad.<br /> <br /> I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> I think the answer presented in the book is the fact that with the Tremere monopoly broken, huge numbers of vampires from varying clans are competing for whatever can be harvested from defunct Tremere chantries and passed around among them. There's limited resources for grimoires, magical components, and other stuff that they're viciously fighting over or trading for scraps regarding.<br /> <br /> So, anyone can learn magic but there's not the formalized training or massive libraries that used to exist before (or at least the Tremere are keeping that on the D-Low). Instead, everyone is basically forced to assemble scrapbooks and share fragments of knowledge. Instead of a dozen master Tremere mages in America, there's a couple of hundred dabblers all trying to become more important and getting an edge.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim don't mind sharing their magic but they're not giving their best stuff. After all, a few level 1-2 rituals can mean the difference between final death and otherwise for a Brujah but mean shit for most Sorcerer Caste.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who is policing it then that makes blood magic have to be the same level as scamming, theft, assassination, drugs and the like?<br /> <br /> I feel like unless someone polices it theres no real reason for Blood Magic to be involved in those things. Which is the confusion for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T21:32:19-07:00","id":1532421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1532404-blood-sigils-question?p=1532417#post1532417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who is policing it then that makes blood magic have to be the same level as scamming, theft, assassination, drugs and the like?<br /> <br /> I feel like unless someone polices it theres no real reason for Blood Magic to be involved in those things. Which is the confusion for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The impression I'm getting is that the reason that all of this is illegal is because vampires are robbing, killing, and cheating each other rather than making sincere deals. You can't trust anyone not to rob you for your magical knowledge or take your money and sell you crap because vampires are all assholes. The opening story is that a couple of Neonates find a torporous Tremere and their response isn't to remove the stake in his heart and expect to be rewarded. Their plan is to steal all of the books in his tomb and diablerize him.<br /> <br /> It's not overtly illegal but its a Wild West where there's very little policing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-12-2024, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T18:03:36-07:00","id":1532626,"title":"","content":"If you need disapproving authorities to justify the underground nature of The Scene, I'd imagine that the early stages of blood sorcery learning involve a lot more &quot;oopsies&quot; than they did when they were mostly happening under experienced Tremere tutelage in spaces designed for that sort of instruction. On a city-by-city basis most princes and other vampire officials likely take a dim view of unpredictable occult disasters happening more frequently at the hands of amateurs. Particularly when the party line is keeping things under wraps to avoid the Second Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}